>   Which kernel is best for multias, the generic or the legacy?
> linux-image-2.6.18-4-alpha-legacy??

The legacy kernel exists solely for the benefit of a handful of machine
types that require a non-standard load address for the kernel.  The only
machines in this category are all AlphaBIOS-only systems that don't support
SRM.

