On Sat, Mar 10, 2007 at 11:52:30AM +0100, Uwe Schindler wrote:

> I have another package self-compiled from source by downloading the source
> package and building it: unrar - I use it since ever on alphy for unpacking
> downloaded rar files, no corrupt extracts, no crashes. Why is this package
> not available on alpha, too?

Because non-free is not autobuilt except in cases that the maintainer has
determined it's acceptable to do so and notifies the experimental/non-free
autobuilding team.

> By the way I have a small problem:
> I have installed libc6.1 and others from experimental (2.3.999), because of
> the pthread problem (fixed by NPTL). But whenever I try to build a package
> it works correctly and when installing the deb file it says that there are
> unmet dependencies: libc-6.1 VERSION 2.4-0 (????)

> How can I fix this somewhere in dpkg and friends? The problem is that
> 2.3.999 of glibc is in reality 2.4. But why does it make a dependency to
> this version and not the real package version?

It's a bug in the experimental glibc package, maybe you could file a bug
report and get the glibc maintainers to fix this?

> I do not want to change the experimental package (it can have bugs, sure),
> but how can I fix this on my machine that apt-get and dpkg do not complain
> all the time? What do I have to change in the package library or the build
> system?

The culprit file is /var/lib/dpkg/info/libc6.1.shlibs, but that's part of
the package and will get overwritten with every update.

